mastery.question_text:
The restricted graphs $y=\sin x$ and $y=\tan x$ are shown on the same axes.
By reflecting both in $y=x$, sketch $y=\arcsin x$ and $y=\arctan x$ for $-1\le x\le1$ and state which curve is higher for $0<x<1$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.5cm, y=0.7cm]
\draw[->] (-2.1,0) -- (2.1,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.9) -- (0,4.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed] (1.5708,-3.7) -- (1.5708,3.7);
\draw[dashed] (-1.5708,-3.7) -- (-1.5708,3.7);
\draw[thick,blue,dashed,domain=-1.2925:1.2925,samples=90,smooth,variable=\t] plot ({\t},{tan(deg(\t))});
\draw[thick,domain=-1.5708:1.5708,samples=80,smooth,variable=\t] plot ({\t},{sin(deg(\t))});
\node[font=\small] at (1.5708,4.15) {$x=\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\node[font=\small] at (-1.5708,4.15) {$x=-\frac{\pi}{2}$};
\node[font=\small,blue] at (0.95,-2.6) {$y=\tan x$};
\node[font=\small] at (-1.05,1.9) {$y=\sin x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.solution_text:
Reflect the endpoints and a key point of each restricted graph in $y=x$.
$\left(\frac{\pi}{2},1\right)\to\left(1,\frac{\pi}{2}\right)$ on $y=\arcsin x$
$\left(\frac{\pi}{4},1\right)\to\left(1,\frac{\pi}{4}\right)$ on $y=\arctan x$
Both curves pass through the origin, and at $x=1$ the arcsin value $\frac{\pi}{2}$ is larger than the arctan value $\frac{\pi}{4}$.
$y=\arcsin x$ is higher for $0<x<1$.
[tikz]
